    <title>ZSA typing challenge issue</title>
    <id>https://pype.dev/zsa-typing-challenge-issue/</id>
    <updated>2025-06-13T08:07:41Z</updated>
    <published>2025-06-13T08:07:41Z</published>
    <link href="https://pype.dev/zsa-typing-challenge-issue/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link>
    <summary type="text">I love zsa and have been using a moonlander for a few years now.</summary>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1 id=&#34;zsa&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;ZSA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I love &lt;a href=&#34;https://zsa.io&#34;&gt;zsa&lt;/a&gt; and have been using a moonlander for a few years now.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;They recently launched &lt;a href=&#34;https://typ.ing&#34;&gt;typ.ing&lt;/a&gt; as a way to train your typing skills - it&amp;rsquo;s a lot like &lt;a href=&#34;https://monkeytype.com&#34;&gt;monkeytype&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a thought about it &lt;a href=&#34;https://thoughts.waylonwalker.com/post/682&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;today-s-challenge&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;Today’s Challenge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#today-s-challenge&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I went to do today&amp;rsquo;s daily challenge and have ran into an issue where part of&#xA;the challenge is to type &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; the forward slash character but it&amp;rsquo;s actually a&#xA;keybind on the website for navigation (well done btw!)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;https://cdn.statically.io/gh/pypeaday/images.pype.dev/main/blog-media/20250613130724_06b0f9ef.png&#34; alt=&#34;20250613130724_06b0f9ef.png&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So when I try to type the challenge I actually bring up the nav menu&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;https://cdn.statically.io/gh/pypeaday/images.pype.dev/main/blog-media/20250613131031_ce06cf48.png&#34; alt=&#34;20250613131031_ce06cf48.png&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So for today I&amp;rsquo;ll take the error on the character to complete it and maybe ZSA&#xA;can look into this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;</content>
